# Token Saving Rules

The user is a student and wants to save cost.

- Keep answers short.
- Do only what was requested.
- Output code only for code requests.
- Show changed files only.
- Do not rewrite the whole project.
- Do not refactor unless asked.
- Keep the existing structure and naming.
- Do not add unrelated suggestions.
- Do not edit too many files at once.
- Do not add new libraries unless necessary.
- Do not add DB, payment, auth, admin, cart, order history, invoice automation, or server features.
- For errors, explain the cause in one line, then provide the minimal fix.
- When the request is large, split the work into small steps and ask for only the next changed files.